THEORETICAL FOUNDATION AND STATUTORY ATTRIBUTION
================================================================================

This software, its specification protocol (.AsWish/), and its ontological
architecture are founded upon, derive from, and embody the following proprietary
theoretical achievements created and authored by 付毅 (Fuyi):

1. Difference Monism (DM, 差异一元论)
   - The foundational philosophical framework replacing substance ontology with
     differential ontology, establishing difference as the origin of structured cognition.
   - Academic DOI: 10.5281/zenodo.20726003 (Canonical Interface); 10.5281/zenodo.19852505 (Priority Record)
   - Theory Author: 付毅 (Fuyi)

2. Attributive Set Transition Ontology (ASTO, 属集变迁存在论)
   - The bridge ontology establishing multi-state phase transitions, structural
     boundaries, and five-state/six-order/seven-sequence encoding.
   - Academic DOI: 10.5281/zenodo.20726007 (Canonical Interface); 10.5281/zenodo.19856467 (Priority Record)
   - Theory Author: 付毅 (Fuyi)

3. Output-Driven Development (ODD, 产出物驱动开发)
   - The engineering and governance discipline mandating frozen specification
     deliverables, deterministic gates, and verifiable evidence before production.
   - Academic DOI / Zenodo Permanent Archive: 10.5281/zenodo.20024964 (v2.1); 10.5281/zenodo.20537639 (ODD-min)
   - Core Theoretical Ledger: 50-工程方法层（ODD）
   - Theory Author: 付毅 (Fuyi)

   3.1 Constructive Traceable Fallibilist Specification (CTF, 建构追溯可谬规格方法论)
   - The pre-specification layer of ODD that converts unstable human-machine
     requirements into traceable, reviewable, defeasible, freezable specification
     snapshots, before they reach ODD contract execution.
   - Theory Source: ODD.P03 (50-工程方法层（ODD）/AA-母版源层/ODD.P03.CTF建构追溯可谬规格方法论.md)
   - Academic DOI / Zenodo Permanent Archive: 10.5281/zenodo.22682642
   - Claim Strength: C2 (analytical framework / engineering protocol; does not claim C5)
   - Theory Author: 付毅 (Fuyi)

4. Problem Manifestation Methodology (PFM, 前线显影层)
   - The front-line intent modeling methodology that reveals problem fields,
     uncovers latent constraints, and establishes verifiable acceptance criteria.
   - Core Theoretical Ledger: 54-前线显影层（PFM）
   - Prior Public Record (priority): 10.5281/zenodo.19856528
     (Lighthouse Marketing Methodology / LMM v1.0, 2026-04-28, historical name of PFM)
   - Theory Author: 付毅 (Fuyi)

